{
  "severity": "critical",
  "host_observations": [
    {"tenant": "corp.onmicrosoft.com", "role": "entra_id_tenant_audited", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:24:08+0200", "last_seen": "2027-09-12T15:31:42+0200"},
    {"ip": "185.220.101.45", "inferred_role": "external_attacker_signin_source_tor_exit", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:28:51+0200", "last_seen": "2027-09-12T15:31:42+0200"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Persistence / Modify Authentication Process — CA Named Location Added", "technique": "T1556.006", "what_happened": "At 2027-09-12 15:24:08 CEST, Microsoft Graph audit log (ingested into Wazuh via the entraid module) captured: data.azuread.activity='Add named location', data.azuread.initiator='admin01@corp.onmicrosoft.com', data.azuread.target.name='Allow-temp-20270912_152408', data.azuread.target.ipRanges=['185.220.101.0/24'], data.azuread.target.isTrusted=true. admin01 created a new IP-based Named Location flagged as 'trusted' containing the CIDR 185.220.101.0/24. This range is a well-known Tor exit-node range (185.220.101.0/24 is listed in the Tor Project's public exit list).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 99541 'Entra ID: Named Location with hostile IP added' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1556.006 because (a) the activity is 'Add named location', (b) isTrusted=true (an exceptional setting — only ~5 trusted named locations exist in this tenant's history), (c) the IP range matches the Tor exit blacklist enriched by the Wazuh CTI integration. The combination is high-fidelity for malicious CA tampering.", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:24:08+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence / Conditional Access Policy Modified", "technique": "T1556.006", "what_happened": "At 15:24:51 CEST (43 seconds after step 1), data.azuread.activity='Update conditional access policy' on policy name 'Block sign-in from non-corp countries' (the corp's primary MFA/geo-fence CA policy), initiator=admin01@corp.onmicrosoft.com. The change: locations.exclude added the new Named Location 'Allow-temp-20270912_152408' — meaning sign-ins originating from 185.220.101.0/24 are now EXEMPTED from the geo-fence AND from MFA enforcement that the policy chains. data.azuread.modifiedProperties shows the literal diff: old_value (no excluded locations) → new_value (excluded: ['Allow-temp-20270912_152408']).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 99540 'Entra ID: CA policy modified' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1556.006. The 43-second gap between Named Location add (step 1) and CA policy modify (step 2) is the attacker chaining the two operations in a single session. The 'locations.exclude' modification is the specific pattern that BYPASSES MFA enforcement for the named range without alerting users.", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:24:51+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts: Cloud — Sign-in from Tor with MFA Bypassed", "technique": "T1078.004", "what_happened": "At 15:28:51 CEST (4 minutes after the CA policy change), data.azuread.activity='User signed-in', data.azuread.user.upn='ceo@corp.onmicrosoft.com', data.azuread.source_ip='185.220.101.45', data.azuread.country='NL', data.azuread.signin.ConditionalAccess='NotApplied', data.azuread.signin.MFADetail='MFASkipped', data.azuread.signin.result='Success'. The CEO's account just signed in from a Tor exit node — the attacker is using a compromised CEO credential — and BOTH the geo-fence AND MFA were bypassed because the attacker pre-created the CA exception in steps 1 and 2. ConditionalAccess=NotApplied is the literal smoking-gun field: the corp's MFA policy was DEFANGED by the attacker's own change 4 minutes earlier.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 99542 'Sign-in succeeds from newly-trusted IP <5 min after CA change' fired with rule.mitre.id=[T1556.006,T1078.004] correlating: (a) the source IP 185.220.101.45 falls within the 185.220.101.0/24 added in step 1, (b) the sign-in occurred <5 minutes after the CA policy modification, (c) ConditionalAccess=NotApplied AND MFADetail=MFASkipped — both controls bypassed.", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:28:51+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Audit Log Cleanup Attempt", "technique": "T1070", "what_happened": "At 15:31:42 CEST (~3 min after the CEO sign-in), admin01 deleted the Named Location 'Allow-temp-20270912_152408' via Microsoft Graph DELETE call: data.azuread.activity='Delete named location'. The attacker is removing the IP range from the tenant's current state to hide the persistence path before further investigation. BUT: the AuditLogs entries from steps 1, 2 are immutable in Entra ID's audit store (Microsoft retains for 30+ days) — the cleanup deletes the live CA configuration but NOT the audit history. Detection succeeded BECAUSE the audit logs were already in Wazuh.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule 99543 'Entra ID: Named Location deleted soon after creation (<10 min)' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1070 — the operator-skill fingerprint of an attacker covering their tracks after using the exception window.", "first_seen": "2027-09-12T15:31:42+0200"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2027-09-12T15:24:08+0200", "end": "2027-09-12T15:31:42+0200"},
